        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Tokenizes the source text into tokens using the `Simplified Maximal Munch`_ algorithm
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The context for the source text to be tokenized </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>includeFiltered</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Ignored by this base class -- exists so a subclass like :cpp:class:`FilteredTokenizer`
can thread its own &quot;include the otherwise-filtered tokens&quot; flag through this same,
shared loop via :cpp:func:`acceptToken` (which *does* look at it), rather than every
subclass having to reimplement the whole loop just to pass one extra value along
</verbatim></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
